    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0313" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 851.857/55</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 21, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 7.45 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5732. Consul, Southampton, is forwarding to Department affidavit of four seamen,
                    George Goldrainer, Fred O’Neill, Clarence Barrett, <pb facs="0314" n="142"
                        xml:id="pg142"/> Edward Staples, claiming American citizenship, members crew
                    French sailing ship <hi rendition="#italic">Bayonne</hi>, from New York,
                    December 28, for England, cargo wheat. Submarine signaled ship stop February 17,
                    4.30 afternoon, 25 miles off starting point; crew took to boats, weather calm,
                    foggy. Submarine of German nationality took provisions from ship and blew her
                    up. Germans provisioned ship’s boats, lights of five steamers visible, crew
                    reached land in 17 hours. <hi rendition="#italic">Bayonne</hi> did not attempt
                    escape or resist.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
